  "body": "## Summary\n\n  `_getPersonalUtilizationRatio` contains a documented first-timer protection:\n\n  \"If the user had nothing claimable last epoch, don't penalize them as it's their first ever claim\"\n\n  This protection is structurally unreachable for users who lock veTRUST but do not interact with the MultiVault, because the\n  delta-based early-return fires first. Every new veTRUST locker who does not deposit in the MultiVault during their first claimable\n  epoch receives personalUtilizationLowerBound (30%) instead of the intended 100%, losing 70% of their first epoch's rewards to the\n  protocol sweep.\n\n  ---\n  ## Vulnerability Detail\n\n  personalUtilization in MultiVault is only modified by `_addUtilization` (called on deposit) and `_removeUtilization` (called on redeem).\n  A user who never calls deposit or redeem always has `personalUtilization[user][*] = 0`.\n\n  getUserUtilizationInEpoch returns personalUtilization[user][history[0]] where history[0] is the most recent active epoch. For a pure\n  veTRUST holder with no MultiVault activity, this is always 0 for every epoch query.\n\n  Control flow in _getPersonalUtilizationRatio for a pure veTRUST holder:\n\n  userUtilizationBefore = getUserUtilizationInEpoch(user, epoch-1) = 0\n  userUtilizationAfter  = getUserUtilizationInEpoch(user, epoch)   = 0\n  rawUtilizationDelta   = 0 - 0 = 0\n\n  Line 516: if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0)          ← fires ALWAYS\n  Line 517:     return personalUtilizationLowerBound  ← returns 30%, DONE\n               // Lines 526-529 never evaluated\n\n  The protected codepath (lines 526–529) requires rawUtilizationDelta > 0:\n\n  ```solidity\nif (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) {\n      return personalUtilizationLowerBound;   // line 517 — early return\n  }\n  // Only reachable with delta > 0:\n  if (userUtilizationTarget == 0) {\n      // \"don't penalize them as it's their first ever claim\"\n      if (_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1) == 0) {\n          return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;   // 100% — UNREACHABLE for pure veTRUST holders\n      }\n      return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n  }\n```\n\n  Exact scenario where the design intent is violated:\n\n  Consider Alice who locks 100,000 wrapped TRUST in epoch N (first-ever lock), claims for epoch N in epoch N+1, and never touches\n  MultiVault:\n\n  - eligible[epoch N-1] = 0 (she had no veTRUST before epoch N)\n  - userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[Alice][epoch N-1] = 0 (never claimed)\n  - rawUtilizationDelta = 0 (no MultiVault activity)\n\n  Line 517 fires. Alice receives 30%.\n\n  The first-timer condition at lines 526–529 would return 100% IF delta were > 0: target == 0 AND eligible[prev] == 0 — exactly Alice's\n   situation. But the delta check blocks evaluation.\n\n  Bob in the same epoch with the same lock size, but also deposits 1 ETH into MultiVault:\n  - delta > 0 (the deposit incremented his personalUtilization)\n  - reaches lines 526–529: target == 0, eligible[prev] == 0 → returns 100%\n\n  Scope limitation (important for severity):\n  - This 70% loss only applies to a user's first claimable epoch where they have zero prior veTRUST balance in the previous epoch.\n  - In all subsequent epochs, personalUtilizationLowerBound (30%) is the intended behavior for users not growing their MultiVault\n  position (delta = 0 with prior claim history → correct).\n  - If the user had veTRUST in the previous epoch but did not claim, they fall into the \"chose not to claim\" branch regardless of the\n  delta check, so the first-timer protection would not have applied anyway.\n\n  ---\n  ## Impact\n\n  Every new veTRUST locker who does not interact with MultiVault during their first claimable epoch loses 70% of that epoch's rewards\n  to the protocol sweep.\n\n  Example (default test configuration):\n  - Alice locks 100,000 wTRUST, sole locker in epoch N\n  - emissionsForEpoch(N) = 1000 TRUST (system utilization ratio assumed 100% for simplicity)\n  - Alice's eligible raw rewards ≈ 490 TRUST\n  - Expected (per code comment): 490 TRUST × 100% = 490 TRUST\n  - Actual (bug): 490 TRUST × 30% = 147 TRUST\n  - Lost to protocol sweep: 343 TRUST (70%)\n\n  The user has no recourse. No admin action can retroactively correct the claim.\n\n  ---\n ## Recommended Fix\n\n  Move the first-timer eligibility check to also execute in the delta <= 0 branch:\n```solidity\n   if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) {\n  -    return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n  +    // Still apply the first-timer protection for genuine new claimants\n  +    if (userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[_account][_epoch - 1] == 0\n  +        && _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1) == 0) {\n  +        return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR; // 100%\n  +    }\n  +    return personalUtilizationLowerBound;\n   }\n```\n\n  This preserves the existing penalty for:\n  - Users who had eligible rewards last epoch but chose not to claim (eligible[prev] > 0, target == 0)\n  - Users with established claim history but no position growth (target > 0, delta = 0)",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\n  Both tests in tests/PoCCore.t.sol pass without modification:\n\n  forge test --match-contract PoCCore -vv\n\n  Output:\n  [PASS] test_submissionValidity() — Alice ratio: 3000 (floor), Bob ratio: 10000 (100%)\n  [PASS] test_permanentFloorForPureVeTrustHolder() — Charlie epochs 2-6: ratio always 3000\n\n  test_submissionValidity proves the direct contrast:\n  - Alice (pure veTRUST, locks epoch 0, claims epoch 2) → 30%\n  - Bob (locks epoch 2 AND deposits MultiVault epoch 2, zero prior balance) → 100%\n  - Both are first-time claimers with eligible[prev] == 0, target == 0\n\n  test_permanentFloorForPureVeTrustHolder proves the first-epoch damage by showing Charlie's ratio never rises above floor for any\n  epoch ≥ 2.\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title  PoCCore\n * @notice Medium Finding: First-time claimant 100% personal-utilization-ratio bonus\n *         is permanently unreachable for pure veTRUST holders (no MultiVault interaction).\n *\n *  ROOT CAUSE — TrustBonding._getPersonalUtilizationRatio (lines ~516–534):\n *\n *    // Step 1 — fires for ALL users with no MultiVault activity:\n *    if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0)\n *        return personalUtilizationLowerBound;   // ← EARLY RETURN, 30%\n *\n *    // Step 2 — ONLY reachable when delta > 0:\n *    if (userUtilizationTarget == 0) {\n *        // \"don't penalize them as it's their first ever claim\"\n *        if (_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(account, epoch-1) == 0)\n *            return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;  // 100% ← PERMANENTLY UNREACHABLE for delta==0 path\n *    }\n *\n *  personalUtilization is only modified by MultiVault deposit/redeem.\n *  A pure veTRUST holder's delta is always 0 → Step 1 always fires → Step 2 never reached.\n *\n *  IMPACT:\n *  Pure veTRUST holders permanently receive personalUtilizationLowerBound (30%) for EVERY\n *  epoch they claim, regardless of lock amount, lock duration, or whether it is their first\n *  ever claim. The 30% is not redistributed; it is swept by the protocol after the window.\n *  A user locking 100 000 TRUST for 2 years loses 70% of their rewards on every single epoch.\n *\n *  CONTRAST (shows the reachable path):\n *  A user who locks veTRUST with zero previous-epoch balance AND deposits in MultiVault in the\n *  same epoch correctly receives 100%: delta > 0 allows Step 2 to run, and eligible[epoch-1] == 0\n *  triggers the first-timer protection.\n */\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n\n    uint256 internal constant EPOCH_LEN = 14 days; // matches BaseTest config\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        vm.deal(address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController), 10_000_000 ether);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Core PoC.\n     *\n     * Timeline:\n     *   Epoch 0 (ts < epoch0End): Alice locks veTRUST.\n     *   Epoch 2 (ts >= epoch1End): Bob locks veTRUST AND deposits in MultiVault.\n     *   Epoch 3 (ts >= epoch2End): Both claim for epoch 2.\n     *\n     * Alice: has veTRUST since epoch 0, no MultiVault → delta == 0 → floor (30%)\n     * Bob:   zero veTRUST in epoch 1, deposits in epoch 2 → delta > 0, eligible[epoch1]==0 → 100%\n     *\n     * Both are first-time claimers (never claimed before). Per the NatSpec comment both should\n     * receive 100%. Only Bob does.\n     */\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 startTs = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(0) - EPOCH_LEN; // epoch 0 start\n        // Sanity: we are in epoch 0 at test start (block.timestamp < epoch0End)\n        // BaseTest setUp already warps to block.timestamp + 20; still epoch 0 given\n        // TRUST_BONDING_START_TIMESTAMP = block.timestamp + 20 from BaseTest.\n\n        // ── Epoch 0: Alice locks veTRUST only ─────────────────────────────────\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), 100_000 ether);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(100_000 ether, block.timestamp + 2 * 365 days);\n\n        // ── Jump to epoch 2 (skipping epoch 1) ───────────────────────────────\n        // epoch1End = startTimestamp + 2 * epochLen\n        uint256 epoch1End = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(1);\n        vm.warp(epoch1End + 1); // now in epoch 2\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 2, \"should be epoch 2\");\n\n        // ── Epoch 2: Bob locks veTRUST AND deposits into MultiVault ───────────\n        // Bob has zero veTRUST balance in epoch 1 → eligible[epoch1] == 0 for Bob\n        resetPrank(users.bob);\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), 100_000 ether);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(100_000 ether, block.timestamp + 2 * 365 days);\n\n        // Create an atom (needed for deposit target) and deposit\n        bytes32 atomId = createSimpleAtom(\"poc\", protocol.multiVault.getAtomCost(), users.admin);\n        resetPrank(users.bob);\n        protocol.multiVault.deposit{ value: 1 ether }(users.bob, atomId, 1, 0);\n\n        // ── Advance to epoch 3: claim epoch 2 ────────────────────────────────\n        uint256 epoch2End = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(2);\n        vm.warp(epoch2End + 1); // now in epoch 3\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 3, \"should be epoch 3\");\n        uint256 claimEp = 2; // epoch 2 is previous epoch\n\n        // ── Read personal utilization ratios ─────────────────────────────────\n        uint256 floor  = protocol.trustBonding.personalUtilizationLowerBound(); // 3000 = 30%\n        uint256 maxBP  = protocol.trustBonding.BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR();          // 10000 = 100%\n        uint256 aliceR = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.alice, claimEp);\n        uint256 bobR   = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.bob,   claimEp);\n\n        console2.log(\"Claiming epoch:\", claimEp);\n        console2.log(\"Floor (30%):\", floor, \" Max (100%):\", maxBP);\n        console2.log(\"Alice (pure veTRUST) ratio:\", aliceR);\n        console2.log(\"Bob   (veTRUST + MultiVault) ratio:\", bobR);\n\n        // ── BUG: Alice is a first-timer but receives only floor (30%) ─────────\n        assertEq(aliceR, floor,\n            \"BUG: pure veTRUST first-timer gets floor, not 100%\");\n\n        // ── CORRECT: Bob (delta > 0, zero epoch-1 eligible) receives 100% ─────\n        assertEq(bobR, maxBP,\n            \"Bob (veTRUST + MultiVault first-timer) gets 100%\");\n\n        // ── Quantify the per-epoch reward loss for Alice ──────────────────────\n        uint256 raw    = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, claimEp);\n        uint256 actual = raw * aliceR / maxBP;  // 30% of raw\n        uint256 loss   = raw - actual;          // 70% of raw lost to protocol sweep\n\n        console2.log(\"Alice raw eligible rewards:\", raw);\n        console2.log(\"Alice actual (30%):\", actual, \"  lost (70%):\", loss);\n\n        assertGt(raw, 0, \"Alice must have eligible rewards\");\n        assertLt(actual, raw, \"Alice receives less than she deserves\");\n        // loss ≈ 70% of raw (small rounding diff acceptable)\n        assertApproxEqAbs(loss, raw * (maxBP - floor) / maxBP, 1);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Pure veTRUST holders get floor on EVERY epoch, not just the first.\n    function test_permanentFloorForPureVeTrustHolder() external {\n        resetPrank(users.charlie);\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), 50_000 ether);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(50_000 ether, block.timestamp + 2 * 365 days);\n\n        uint256 floor = protocol.trustBonding.personalUtilizationLowerBound();\n        uint256 maxBP = protocol.trustBonding.BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR();\n\n        // Check epochs 2–6: Charlie always gets floor\n        for (uint256 ep = 2; ep <= 6; ep++) {\n            uint256 epEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(ep);\n            vm.warp(epEnd + 1); // advance into epoch ep+1\n\n            uint256 eligible = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.charlie, ep);\n            if (eligible == 0) continue;\n\n            uint256 r = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.charlie, ep);\n            console2.log(\"Charlie epoch, ratio, floor:\", ep, r, floor);\n            assertEq(r, floor, \"pure veTRUST holder always gets floor\");\n            assertLt(r, maxBP, \"floor is strictly less than max\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\noutput\n```solidity\n$forge test --match-contract PoCCore -vvv\n[⠊] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 2 tests for tests/PoCCore.t.sol:PoCCore\n[PASS] test_permanentFloorForPureVeTrustHolder() (gas: 694478)\nLogs:\n  MultiVault implementation address:  0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a\n  MultiVault proxy address:  0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  AtomWallet implementation deployed at: 0xc7183455a4C133Ae270771860664b6B7ec320bB1\n  AtomWalletBeacon deployed at: 0xa0Cb889707d426A7A386870A03bc70d1b0697598\n  AtomWalletFactory implementation address:  0x1d1499e622D69689cdf9004d05Ec547d650Ff211\n  AtomWalletFactory proxy address:  0xA4AD4f68d0b91CFD19687c881e50f3A00242828c\n  WrappedTrust address:  0x03A6a84cD762D9707A21605b548aaaB891562aAb\n  TrustBonding implementation address:  0xD6BbDE9174b1CdAa358d2Cf4D57D1a9F7178FBfF\n  TrustBonding proxy address:  0x15cF58144EF33af1e14b5208015d11F9143E27b9\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Implementation 0x212224D2F2d262cd093eE13240ca4873fcCBbA3C\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Proxy 0x2a07706473244BC757E10F2a9E86fB532828afe3\n  BondingCurveRegistry address:  0xD16d567549A2a2a2005aEACf7fB193851603dd70\n  LinearCurve address:  0x3381cD18e2Fb4dB236BF0525938AB6E43Db0440f\n  OffsetProgressiveCurve address:  0x1aF7f588A501EA2B5bB3feeFA744892aA